# NOT COMMITTED, and this is the same disposition the technical calibration gives
# its harvest cache: a regenerable convenience is never committed, and the
# committed evidence is the RESULTS files and the record.
#
#   filings/*.pdf   ARCC's own documents, 88MB. Re-retrievable at any time by
#                   `python3 fetch_sources.py`, and fetch_attempts.json holds the
#                   URL, timestamp, byte count and sha256 of every one — so the
#                   integrity of what was read is on the record even though the
#                   bytes are not in the repository.
#   ocr/*.png       300dpi renders of the scanned filings, 280MB. Pure
#                   intermediate: `python3 ocr_statements.py` regenerates them.
#
# THE OCR TEXT IS COMMITTED. ocr/*.txt is what was actually read off the pixels
# and is the evidence behind every figure in panel.py — a reader must be able to
# check the transcription without re-running anything.
filings/*.pdf
ocr/*.png
__pycache__/
